            <ArticleTitle>Diltiazem hydrochloride.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>413-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Since their introduction in 1963, calcium-channel blockers, with their effectiveness and lack of side effects, have become widely used. Diltiazem hydrochloride, a benzothiazine, has its major role in the treatment of angina and is also used as an antihypertensive and antiarrhythmic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
